the-firm-as-one-program-lines-4 : List (List Word)
the-firm-as-one-program-lines-4 = cons "- **O1** Open with the CitSec superorganism and the Jane Street superorganism." (cons "- **O2** First the human element: the upper echelon of engineering and computer-science talent, concentrated in one superorganism around a well-defined problem: make money with machines." (cons "  - **O2.1** Most organizations dilute talent across vague goals; these point all of it at one unambiguous objective." (cons "  - **O2.2** Every idea is tested against PnL within days: an unusually tight and honest feedback loop on intelligence." (cons "  - **O2.3** So every part of computer science is pushed to its limit here under one measure: compilers, distributed systems, hardware, numerics, networking, formal reasoning. See [O7]." (cons "- **O3** Collaborative intelligence, the value of information interactions, variance of expertise, choice of tool, focus of problem space." (cons "  - **O3.1** Where these interactions go when the firm is one program: [C3], [C16], [C17]." (cons "- **O4** This leads to the unique choices of these businesses: CitSec's C++ platform, Jane Street's OCaml platform." (cons "  - **O4.1** Jane Street: OCaml, chosen for correctness that a large group reviewing one another's code can rely on." (cons (quoted (cons "    - **O4.1.1** " (cons "Make illegal states unrepresentable" (cons " (Yaron Minsky): correctness is a property of the code everyone reads, not of the people who wrote it." nil)))) (cons "    - **O4.1.2** Pushed into everything: Async and Core libraries, HardCaml for FPGA design, and OxCaml (unboxed types, stack allocation, modes)." (cons "    - **O4.1.3** A firm built on correctness, reaching for control of the machine." (cons "  - **O4.2** Citadel Securities: C++, chosen for total control over layout, allocation and latency." (cons "    - **O4.2.1** Templates as a compile-time language for specialization. See [P5], [C4]." (cons "    - **O4.2.2** No proofs and pervasive undefined behaviour, so correctness rests on conventions, tests and review discipline." (cons "    - **O4.2.3** A firm built on control, reaching for correctness." (cons "  - **O4.3** Each firm bet on one half of the problem and now spends heavily to recover the other half." (cons "- **O5** Then: what these languages are worth and what they enable." (cons "  - **O5.1** OCaml enables a large group to trust shared code through types; C++ enables the last nanosecond. See [O4]." (cons "- **O6** Then: what a language requires to support these desiderata." (cons "  - **O6.1** Meaning precise enough to reason about: OCaml's types are the start, dependent types with proofs the end. [P2]" (cons "  - **O6.2** Control of the machine as defined meaning: layout, allocation, timing and hardware as definitions with semantics, not escape hatches. [P6], [P7]" (cons "  - **O6.3** Staging and specialization in the language itself: templates and HardCaml generators are partial evaluation without a correctness relation; the Futamura projections with proofs are the complete form. [P5]" (cons "  - **O6.4** One language across the whole firm: HardCaml shows Jane Street wanting strategy, tooling and circuits in one language. [C1]" (cons "  - **O6.5** End-to-end optimization. [O7]" (cons "  - **O6.6** Jane Street got correctness and is fighting for control; Citadel Securities got control and is fighting for correctness; the cubical core makes both definitions of one language. [P2], [P6]" (cons "- **O7** Nothing in computer science is not developed fully here; this was the three-year study of the industry before execution. Optimization, end-to-end optimization." (cons "  - **O7.1** You can only optimize across a boundary whose two sides you can relate. Today every boundary blocks optimization: team to team, language to language, process to process, software to silicon." (cons "  - **O7.2** The optimum of the whole is not the sum of local optima, so the firm is locally optimal and globally wasteful." (cons "  - **O7.3** With the whole firm as one program, computable equality to swap representations and specialization that carries proofs, strategy, parser, NIC and photon are optimized as one object. [C4], [C15], [S1]" (cons "" nil))))))))))))))))))))))))))))))
